{"base_rate":0.24540682414698162,"brier":0.09038503937007875,"bss":0.5119132220413858,"bss_hi":0.6101463516786166,"bss_lo":0.4041253817679802,"chart":{"base":[274.1,104.4],"fp":[271.3,261.1],"lead":"62,277.1 272,254.6 482,215.3 692,147","note":{"base":"skill 0.51 — higher than 93% of cities","fp":"low end +3pp, high end +10pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 87% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 3%; promised 91% → rained 82%"},"rel":"66.3,454.2 241,343.7 633.6,111.5"},"country":"ES","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.05191601049868771,"ess":355.037225072907,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Madrid</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Madrid rain forecast is strongly skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>95%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 762 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nMADRID - RETIRO, 2.1 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.51, ranked 16 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(5&ndash;55) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>360</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'><b>25%</b></td><td class='num'>92</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>44%</td><td class='num'><b>32%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>69%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>95%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Madrid</b> <span class=\"muted\">Spain</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Strongly skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;25% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 25% of days.</p><p>The forecast did far better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.51</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>5&ndash;55\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>762 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Madrid &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Madrid\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 71.1865,350.15 114.10130434782609,298.9130434782609 213.85567567567568,180.32432432432432 347.64461538461546,55.333333333333314 410.7292307692308,18.0 410.7292307692308,27.333333333333314 347.64461538461546,116.0 213.85567567567568,263.94594594594594 114.10130434782609,350.3478260869565 71.1865,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"292.6719160104987\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"292.6719160104987\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,373.9111111111111 71.1865,363.8 114.10130434782609,291.0 213.85567567567568,263.94594594594594 347.64461538461546,130.0 410.7292307692308,36.666666666666686\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 360 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"373.9111111111111\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"71.1865\" cy=\"363.8\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 16%&amp;#10;It rained 25% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 92 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"114.10130434782609\" cy=\"291.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 44%&amp;#10;It rained 32% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"213.85567567567568\" cy=\"263.94594594594594\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 82%&amp;#10;It rained 69% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"347.64461538461546\" cy=\"130.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 95% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.7292307692308\" cy=\"36.666666666666686\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(25%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Madrid the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.58) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.32).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>19%</td><td class='num'>0.324</td><td class='num'>8.2%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'>0.380</td><td class='num'>0.9%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>33%</td><td class='num'>0.548</td><td class='num'>3.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.575</td><td class='num'>3.5%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":40.4165,"lon":-3.70256,"n":762,"n_cities":216,"name":"Madrid","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":360,"obs":0.022222222222222223,"sig":true},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.037250000000000005,"n":80,"obs":0.05,"sig":false},{"hi":0.3,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.1584782608695652,"n":92,"obs":0.25,"sig":true},{"hi":0.63,"lo":0.3,"mean":0.44027027027027027,"n":74,"obs":0.32432432432432434,"sig":false},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.63,"mean":0.8182051282051284,"n":78,"obs":0.6923076923076923,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.98,"mean":0.9964102564102566,"n":78,"obs":0.9487179487179487,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":2.1,"provisional":false,"rank":16,"rank_hi":55.02499999999998,"rank_lo":5.0,"reliability":0.004422493756693524,"resolution":0.09922602235671862,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"madrid","station":"MADRID - RETIRO","timezone":"Europe/Madrid"}